#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:1
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:3
msgid ""
"A directory that contains links to profiles managed by [`nix-env`](../../"
"command-ref/nix-env.md) and [`nix profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"profile.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:5
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles` for regular users"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:6
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root` if the user is `root`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:8
msgid "A profile is a directory of symlinks to files in the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:10
msgid "Filesystem layout"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:12
msgid ""
"Profiles are versioned as follows. When using a profile named _path_, _path_ "
"is a symlink to _path_`-`_N_`-link`, where _N_ is the version of the "
"profile. In turn, _path_`-`_N_`-link` is a symlink to a path in the Nix "
"store. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:24
msgid "Each of these symlinks is a root for the Nix garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:26
msgid ""
"The contents of the store path corresponding to each version of the profile "
"is a tree of symlinks to the files of the installed packages, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:53
msgid "Each profile version contains a manifest file:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:54
msgid ""
"[`manifest.nix`](../../command-ref/files/manifest.nix.md) used by [`nix-env`]"
"(../../command-ref/nix-env.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:55
msgid ""
"[`manifest.json`](../../command-ref/files/manifest.json.md) used by [`nix "
"profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md) (experimental)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:57
msgid "User profile link"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:59
msgid "A symbolic link to the user's current profile:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:61
msgid "`~/.nix-profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:62
msgid ""
"`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profile` if [`use-xdg-base-directories`](../../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories) is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:64
msgid "By default, this symlink points to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:66
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/profile` for regular users"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:67
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/profile` for `root`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/profiles.md:69
msgid ""
"The `PATH` environment variable should include `/bin` subdirectory of the "
"profile link (e.g. `~/.nix-profile/bin`) for the user environment to be "
"visible to the user. The [installer](../../installation/installing-binary."
"md) sets this up by default, unless you enable [`use-xdg-base-directories`]"
"(../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories)."
msgstr ""
